@startuml deployment
title Deployment diagram: local desktop MVP (no hosted node)\nFR-005, FR-006, FR-017; NFR-002, NFR-006, NFR-010; FR-044 to FR-046 shown only as deferred context
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 50
left to right direction

actor "Member\n(one signed-in session at a time)" as Member

node "Member computer (Windows, macOS or Linux)" as PC {
  node "Java 21 runtime (JVM)" as JVM {
    artifact "splitsmart.jar\n(executable JAR, one Maven module;\nH2 driver bundled)" as Jar
    artifact "db/migration/V001~_~_initial.sql\n(ordered numbered scripts, inside the JAR)" as Scripts
  }

  folder "Selected data directory\n(--data-dir, default <U+007E>/.splitsmart)" as DataDir {
    file "app.lock\nexclusive owner lock,\nheld for the process lifetime" as Lock
    database "splitsmart.mv.db (H2 file)\naccounts (PBKDF2 hashes only), groups,\nexpenses, shares, decisions, payments,\nnotifications, lifecycle events,\noperation results, schema_version,\nin-progress migration marker" as H2
    folder "receipts/\nfinal files named by generated UUID" as Receipts
    folder "receipts/staging/\nvalidated bytes before finalize" as Staging
    file "logs/\ntechnical causes only; no passwords,\nno receipt contents" as Logs
  }

  folder "Backup copy\n(whole data directory copied\nafter the application has exited)" as Backup
  folder "Restore directory\n(separate --data-dir;\noriginal kept unchanged)" as Restore
}

Member --> Jar : Swing UI
Jar --> Lock : 1. acquire before opening H2
Jar --> H2 : 2. validate or migrate schema,\nthen JDBC (embedded, file mode)
Jar ..> Scripts : reads
Jar --> Staging : 3. stage receipt
Staging --> Receipts : 4. atomic move on the same\nfile system, then DB reference commits
Jar --> Logs
DataDir ..> Backup : clean shutdown, then copy\n(also taken before any upgrade)
Backup ..> Restore : copy into a new directory,\nopen with --data-dir, verify

note right of Lock
  Second instance: lock unavailable ->
  refuse safely; never open the store.
  Startup failure (unreadable directory or
  database) shows a recovery message and
  never replaces the store (US1-AS8, NFR-010).
end note

note right of H2
  First launch: create a NEW empty directory, lock it,
  apply V001. Reopen: validate version and checksum.
  Upgrade: closed-store backup, durable in-progress
  marker, run script, record version and checksum,
  clear marker. A failed or interrupted migration
  blocks startup; recover from the pre-upgrade backup.
  Unknown future version or checksum mismatch: refuse
  without overwriting (D-5).
end note

note right of Restore
  Verify accounts, memberships, decisions,
  lifecycle history, payment states, derived
  balances, schema version and every referenced
  receipt before adopting the restored copy
  (NFR-006, US1-AS11).
end note

note as Deferred
  DEFERRED, not delivered by this MVP:
  web client (FR-044), Android app (FR-045),
  iOS app (FR-046), web availability (NFR-008),
  cross-client consistency (NFR-009).
  A future release would add a server around
  the same service layer; no hosted node exists here.
end note
@enduml
